    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe placement and decomposition are otherwise idiomatic \u2014 the mapper is already the home for read-time derived fields (`toFiscalYear`, `toSelfLink`, `toIdentityKey`, \u2026), each a `toXxx` default method, and `toRiskFlag`/`hasDisposableAdjacentEmail` follow that pattern exactly, reusing the existing `hasEmail` helper. One structural issue:\n\n**The disposable-provider list is duplicated as a disconnected second source of truth.** The controller already owns the authoritative blocklist:\n\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS = Set.of(\"mailinator.com\", \"tempmail.com\", \"guerrillamail.com\")`\n- `OwnerMapper.DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_BASE_LABELS = Set.of(\"mailinator\", \"tempmail\", \"guerrillamail\")`\n\nThe mapper's set is just the controller's set with the TLD stripped, hand-restated. These are not linked in any way, so adding a fourth disposable provider means editing two lists in two units and silently gets the \"disposable-adjacent\" signal wrong if someone updates only one. The mapper's own Javadoc even asserts the relationship (\"the create endpoint's disposable-domain blocklist, keyed by the label immediately before the final TLD\"), but nothing in code enforces it.\n\nThis is exactly the divergence this codebase goes out of its way to prevent elsewhere, and says so repeatedly: `E164PhoneNumbers` is \"the same table the create endpoint validates against, so the two paths cannot diverge\"; `toIdentityKey` is \"the single source of truth \u2026 so the value clients see is exactly the value that governs rejection\"; `fiscalYear` is \"the single source of truth.\" A maintainer here would expect the base labels to be *derived* from the one authoritative blocklist rather than maintained in parallel.\n\nSuggested fix (either):\n- Derive the base labels from the authoritative set at one point (strip each domain's final TLD label), so there is a single list to maintain; or\n- Extract the disposable-domain list to a shared util (as `E164PhoneNumbers`/`IdentityKeyUtils` already do) that both the create endpoint and the mapper reference, with the base-label view computed from it.",
